  <title>The main window</title>

  <p>The main window opens when PyGtk Posting starts. Its title shows the
  company whose books are open. Every window of the program is in its menus;
  the buttons below them are shortcuts to the windows used every day.</p>

  <section id="buttons">
  <title>The buttons</title>
  <p>The buttons are grouped into <gui>Customer</gui>, <gui>Vendor</gui> and
  <gui>Misc</gui>. The number under a button is how many are waiting:</p>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Draft Invoices</gui></title>
    <p>Invoices not yet posted that have at least one line.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Unpaid Invoices</gui></title>
    <p>Posted invoices not yet paid.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Draft POs</gui></title>
    <p>Purchase orders not yet closed that have at least one line.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Unprocessed Orders</gui></title>
    <p>Closed purchase orders whose vendor invoice has not been entered.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Receive Orders</gui></title>
    <p>Purchase orders invoiced but not yet received.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Documents To Invoice</gui></title>
    <p>Documents marked to be invoiced.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Draft Job Sheets</gui></title>
    <p>Job sheets neither completed nor invoiced.</p></item>
  </terms>
  <p>The numbers change by themselves when an invoice, purchase order, job
  sheet or document changes, on this computer or another one.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="to_do">
  <title>The to-do list</title>
  <p>The <gui>To Do</gui> list collects what is due. Double click a row to
  open the window that deals with it.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p><gui>Print statements</gui> appears from the statement day set in
    <guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Settings</gui></guiseq>, in the month after
    the last statements were made.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Backup database</gui> appears when the last backup is older
    than the backup frequency in the settings. Double clicking it starts the
    backup.</p></item>
    <item><p>A loan payment appears when a loan's next payment is due.</p></item>
    <item><p>Resources marked as to-do appear in the colour of their tag,
    until they are posted.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="admin">
  <title>Administrator windows</title>
  <p>The windows that change how the books are set up, and the
  <gui>Payroll</gui> menu, are greyed out until you choose
  <guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Admin login</gui></guiseq> and enter
  the administrator password. The menu item then reads <gui>Admin
  logout</gui>. The <link xref="zebra_designer"/>, and the <gui>Edit
  mode</gui> of several reports, ask for the password when you use
  them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="keys">
  <title>Keyboard shortcuts</title>
  <p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>I</key></keyseq> opens a new invoice and
  <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>P</key></keyseq> a new purchase order. See
  <link xref="keyboard_shortcuts"/> to give any menu item a shortcut of its
  own.</p>
  </section>

